===Proper noun===
{{ru-proper noun+|Го́спод|nom_sg=Госпо́дь|voc=~и|n=sg|a=an}}

# the [[Lord]], [[God]]
#: {{lang|ru|Го́споди!}} ''([[vocative case|vocative]])'' — ''Good Lord!''
#: {{ru-ux|[[не|Не]] [[давать|дай]] Госпо́дь!|God forbid!|inline=y}}
#: {{ru-ux|Госпо́дь [[он|его́]] [[знать|зна́ет]]!|God only knows!; Who knows?|inline=y}}
#: {{ru-ux|Госпо́дь [[с#Russian|с]] [[ты|тобо́й]]!|Bless you!; ''also:'' Get outta here! (incredulity)|inline=y}}
#: {{ru-ux|Госпо́дь [[с#Russian|с]] [[он|ним]]!|Forget him!|inline=y}}

====Usage notes====
* It's acceptable to pronounce the first letter "{{m|ru|г}}" as /ɣ/ or /ɦ/ in standard Russian for this word. The [[vocative case]] is more likely to be pronounced with /ɣ/ or /ɦ/. <!--I've heard this opinion but not sure, how to check for frequencies. Not sure if Vahagn is right here. User:Atitarev -->

